  "notes": "{解|と}く is a transitive godan verb meaning to solve, untie, or release.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を particle for the object\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {問題|もんだい}を{解|と}く: to solve a problem\n- {紐|ひも}を{解|と}く: to untie a string\n- {誤解|ごかい}を{解|と}く: to clear up a misunderstanding\n- {謎|なぞ}を{解|と}く: to solve a mystery\n- {禁|きん}を{解|と}く: to lift a ban\n\nHOMOPHONE DISTINCTION:\nSeveral verbs read とく use different kanji:\n- {解|と}く: to solve, untie\n- {溶|と}く: to dissolve (in liquid)\n- {説|と}く: to explain, persuade\n- {梳|と}く: to comb (hair)",
